WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.892
[BEEPING]

00:00:05.057 --> 00:00:06.890
SPEAKER: If you're a
data-driven enterprise,

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.620
you've likely been met with
an explosion of data growth

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.720
in recent years and
need to find the best

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.230
way to store all your terabytes
and petabytes at scale.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.380
Google Cloud Storage allows
worldwide storage and retrieval

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.990
of any amount of
data at any time.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.940
You can use Google Cloud Storage
for a range of scenarios,

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.910
including serving
website content,

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.850
storing data for archival
and disaster recovery,

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.190
or distributing large
data objects to users

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.840
via direct download.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.530
In this hands-on lab, Cloud
Storage Qwik Start Console,

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.470
you will learn how to use the
Google Cloud Platform console

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:42.590
to create a storage bucket,
then upload objects,

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:46.490
create folders, and subfolders,
and make those objects publicly

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:47.610
accessible.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:51.380
Data doesn't just mean rows, and
columns, and numbers anymore.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.150
You may want to store
unstructured data

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:57.230
like messages, documents,
multimedia files, web pages,

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:58.520
and so on.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.180
Whatever your storage
requirements are,

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.360
security, availability,
and cost will

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.400
be your three considerations.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.500
Cloud Storage aims to meet
all of these requirements.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.950
Next up on our quest
is Cloud IM Qwik Start.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

